# Usage

The following examples describe the basic usage of the Doxia Converter.

<!-- MACRO{toc|section=1|fromDepth=2|toDepth=2} -->

Command Line Help
-----------------

```
# java -jar target/doxia-converter-${project.version}-shaded.jar -h

usage: doxia-converter [-e] [-f] [-from <arg>] [-h] [-in <arg>] [-inEncoding <arg>] [-out <arg>] [-outEncoding <arg>] [-to
       <arg>] [-v] [-X]

Options:
 -e,--errors           Produce execution error messages.
 -f,--format           Format the output (actually only xml based outputs) to be human readable.
 -from <arg>           From format. If not specified, autodetect it: for a directory, per file by extension, such as .md,
                       .apt, .xml (xdoc), .xhtml or .fml, skipping files already in the target format.
 -h,--help             Display help information.
 -in,--input <arg>     Input file or directory.
 -inEncoding <arg>     Input file encoding. If not specified, try to autodetect it (only works if input is a single file)
 -out,--output <arg>   Output file or directory.
 -outEncoding <arg>    Output file encoding. If not specified, use the input encoding (or autodetected).
 -to <arg>             To format.
 -v,--version          Display version information.
 -X,--debug            Produce execution debug output.

Supported Formats:
 from: apt, fml, xdoc, xhtml, markdown or auto
 to:   apt, xdoc, xhtml, markdown


Supported Encoding:
 UTF-8, UTF-16BE, UTF-16LE, UTF-32BE, UTF-32LE, Shift_JIS, ISO-2022-JP, ISO-2022-CN, ISO-2022-KR, GB18030, EUC-JP, EUC-KR, Big5,
ISO-8859-1, ISO-8859-2, ISO-8859-5, ISO-8859-6, ISO-8859-7, ISO-8859-8-I, ISO-8859-8, windows-1251, windows-1256, KOI8-R,
ISO-8859-9, IBM424_rtl, IBM424_ltr, IBM420_rtl, IBM420_ltr
```

**Note**: The input parameters (i.e. encoding and format) can be autodetected.

Command Line Execution
----------------------

```
# java -jar target/doxia-converter-${project.version}-shaded.jar \
    -in /path/to/xhtml.file \
    -from xhtml \
    -out /path/to/outputdir \
    -to markdown
```

**Note**: The `from` parameter can be empty. In that case, Doxia converter autodetects the format of the `in` file, or of each file in the `in` directory.

Shared Source Directory
-----------------------

Doxia Sitetools can read documents of any format from one directory, `src/site/source`, where the file extension picks the parser. Without `-from`, the converter reads such a directory the same way: `.apt` is APT, `.md` and `.markdown` are Markdown, `.xml` is XDoc, `.xhtml` is XHTML and `.fml` is FML, each optionally followed by `.vm`. Files already in the target format are left alone, and so is an `.xml` file whose root element is not `<document>`.

To convert every remaining document to Markdown in place, keeping the history in Git:

```
# java -jar target/doxia-converter-${project.version}-shaded.jar \
    -in src/site/source \
    -out src/site/source \
    -to markdown \
    -gitMvInputToOutput
```

Use `-removeIn` instead outside Git. Without either, each source stays next to its converted document, and Doxia Sitetools reports the pair as a duplicate page. The conversion stops before writing anything if two documents, such as `usage.apt` and `usage.xml`, would produce the same output file.

Java Usage
----------

```java
String in = "...";
String from = "...";
String out = "...";
String to = "...";

Converter converter = new DefaultConverter();
try
{
    InputFileWrapper input = InputFileWrapper.valueOf( in, from, "ISO-8859-1", converter.getInputFormats() );
    OutputFileWrapper output = OutputFileWrapper.valueOf( out, to, "UTF-8", converter.getOutputFormats() );

    converter.convert( input, output );
}
catch ( UnsupportedFormatException e )
{
    e.printStackTrace();
}
catch ( ConverterException e )
{
    e.printStackTrace();
}
```

Ant Usage
---------

```xml
 <target name="doxia-convert">
     <java
         jar="./lib/doxia-converter-${project.version}-shaded.jar"
         dir="."
         fork="true"
         failonerror="true"
         >

         <arg value="-in"/>
         <arg value="${esc.d}{tdi.apt}"/>

         <arg value="-out"/>
         <arg value="./doc/${esc.d}{tdi.apt}.${esc.d}{doxia.out.extension}"/>

         <arg value="-to"/>
         <arg value="${esc.d}{doxia.out.format}"/>


         <arg value="-from"/>
         <arg value="apt"/>

         <arg value="-f"/>
     </java>
 </target>

 <target name="doc.xhtml">
     <antcall target="doxia-convert">
         <param name = "doxia.out.format" value = "xhtml"/>
         <param name = "doxia.out.extension" value = "html"/>
     </antcall>
 </target>

 <target name="doc">
     <antcall target="doc.xhtml" />
 </target>
```
